Let me put some thought into this... I'm actually inclined to say that while "knowing the right people" might provide an advantage initially, ultimately it boils down to one's work ethic, skills, and meritocratic value. If someone relies too heavily on their connections rather than genuine ability and drive, they're likely doomed for disappointment when those ties aren't enough anymore.



